    "problem_statement": "SQS FIFO queue message processing broken - messages not properly filtered for dead letter queue and group ordering\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen receiving messages from FIFO queues, the message filtering logic appears to be completely bypassed. Messages that should be moved to dead letter queues based on `maxReceiveCount` are being delivered instead, and FIFO group ordering constraints are not being enforced.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport boto3\nimport json\nfrom moto import mock_aws\nfrom uuid import uuid4\n\n@mock_aws\ndef test_dlq_behavior():\n    sqs = boto3.resource('sqs', region_name='us-east-1')\n    \n    # Create DLQ\n    dlq = sqs.create_queue(\n        QueueName=f'{str(uuid4())[0:6]}-dlq.fifo',\n        Attributes={\n            'FifoQueue': 'true',\n            'ContentBasedDeduplication': 'true'\n        }\n    )\n    \n    # Create main queue with DLQ policy\n    main_queue = sqs.create_queue(\n        QueueName=f'{str(uuid4())[0:6]}.fifo',\n        Attributes={\n            'FifoQueue': 'true',\n            'ContentBasedDeduplication': 'true',\n            'RedrivePolicy': json.dumps({\n                'deadLetterTargetArn': dlq.attributes['QueueArn'],\n                'maxReceiveCount': 1\n            }),\n            'VisibilityTimeout': '1'\n        }\n    )\n    \n    # Send message\n    main_queue.send_message(MessageBody='test', MessageGroupId='group1')\n    \n    # Receive message (first time)\n    messages = main_queue.receive_messages()\n    print(f\"First receive: {len(messages)} messages\")  # Should be 1\n    \n    # Wait for visibility timeout\n    import time\n    time.sleep(1.1)\n    \n    # Try to receive again - message should go to DLQ after maxReceiveCount\n    messages = main_queue.receive_messages()\n    print(f\"Second receive from main: {len(messages)} messages\")  # Should be 0\n    \n    # Check DLQ\n    dlq_messages = dlq.receive_messages()\n    print(f\"DLQ messages: {len(dlq_messages)} messages\")  # Should be 1\n\ntest_dlq_behavior()\n```\n\nExpected output:\n```\nFirst receive: 1 messages\nSecond receive from main: 0 messages\nDLQ messages: 1 messages\n```\n\nActual output:\n```\nFirst receive: 1 messages\nSecond receive from main: 1 messages  # Message not moved to DLQ!\nDLQ messages: 0 messages\n```\n\n#### Additional Context\n\nThis also affects FIFO group ordering where messages from the same group should be processed sequentially, but multiple messages from the same group can now be received simultaneously.",
